━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ do type-program
    - session Session
    - workers Int = default-worker-count

` Types the program: on `workers` workers first (`type-in-parallel`), where there are several, and
` then in `session` whatever they left, from the mains of the modules, or all of it where what the
` workers typed is not taken. Where the pass starts over (`check-pass`), it is typed so again.
session.program.note-derived-names()
seed-mains(session)
while true
    if workers > 1
        //+typing.phase// parallel
        type-in-parallel(session, workers)
        //-typing.phase// parallel done
    //+typing.phase// check-pass
    . checked = check-pass(session)
    //-typing.phase// check-pass done
    if checked
        =
    start-over(session)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ do type-in-parallel
    - session Session
    - count Int

` Types the program on `count` workers, each in a type pass of its own, and takes what they typed
` into `session`, which then types whatever is left as it would alone (`merge-sessions`). The
` workers share out the instances that any pass can intern, starting from the mains of the modules
` in the order `seed-mains` gives them, and each takes in what the others published of an instance
` in place of typing it again. Where a pass diverged (`SharedTyping.diverge`), nothing they typed is
` taken, and `session`, which holds only the mains then, types the program as it would alone.
. shared = SharedTyping()
shared.traces-lint = session.facts.traces-lint
shared.tracked = session.panics.tracked-keys()
. program = session.program
. seeded = export-instance(session, seed-main(session, program.entry-module))
if seeded
    shared.offer(seeded)
for position in 0 .. < program.modules.length
    . item = export-instance(session, seed-main(session, position as ModuleId))
    if item
        shared.offer(item)
. passes SyncBufferedChannel'Session
. ended SyncBufferedChannel'Bool
. failure = WorkerFailure()
. pool = Worker(count)
for _ in 0 .. < count
    do (pool) new
        passes <- type-share(program, shared)
        ended <- true
    catch failed
        failure.keep(failed)
        shared.abandon()
        ended <- true
for _ in 0 .. < count
    <- ended
passes.close()
. peers [Session]
for peer in passes
    peers += peer
if !shared.has-diverged()
    //+typing.phase// merge
    merge-sessions(session, peers, pool)
    //-typing.phase// merge done
. released SyncBufferedChannel'Bool
for peer in peers
    do (pool) new
        peer.release()
        released <- true
    catch failed
        failure.keep(failed)
        released <- true
for _ in 0 .. < peers.length
    <- released
pool.stop()
failure.raise-kept()

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ do type-share Session
    - program Program
    - shared SharedTyping

` One worker's type pass: types each instance it takes from those the passes share out, offering
` the others what its typing queues as it goes (`offer-queued`), and types itself those only it can
` intern. One another pass published is left to that pass. One whose errors settle only after its
` body ended is published once they do (`Instances.keeps-settled`). Where no offered instance
` waits to be taken, the functions that answer for others in the tables of the classes and the
` interfaces it has typed are offered too (`ClassTables.find-overrides`,
` `WitnessTables.finding`), and are checked in `session` after the merge. Once a pass diverged,
` what the passes typed is not taken, so what is offered after is taken without typing it.
. session = Session(program)
session.shared = shared
session.instances.keeps-settled = true
session.facts.traces-lint = shared.traces-lint
session.panics.seed(shared.tracked)
. instances = session.instances
. tables = ClassTables(session)
. witnesses = WitnessTables(session)
witnesses.finding = true
. cursor Size = 0
for item in shared.items
    shared.take()
    if !shared.has-diverged() && !shared.has(item.key)
        . id = import-instance(session, item)
        if instances.stable-keys[id] == item.key
            demand-instance(session, id)
    . drained = shared.has-diverged()
    while !drained
        offer-queued(session)
        while cursor < session.local.length
            demand-instance(session, session.local[cursor])
            cursor += 1
            offer-queued(session)
        . queued = instances.worklist.length
        if shared.idle()
            tables.find-overrides()
            expand-witnesses(session, witnesses)
        drained = instances.worklist.length == queued
    shared.finish()
tables.release()
= session
